  "timepicker": {},
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 76,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "End to end, and what an alert is and is not",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**PTS \u2192 alert is the end-to-end number.** It is measured from the sighting's *PTS-derived* timestamp \u2014 the frame's own presentation time plus the stream epoch, never frame arrival time \u2014 to the moment watchlist correlation raised the alert. Two series measure the same quantity from different places: the live histogram comes from the sightings consumer, and the stored quantiles come from `alerts.created_at - alerts.sighting_ts` so the number survives the consumer exiting.\n\n**An alert is a ranked possibility, never an identification.** Every watchlist provider in SAAKSHI is a mock \u2014 there is no live VAHAN, SARTHI, eGujCop, AFIS or NAFIS connectivity \u2014 and no biometric data is processed anywhere. A fuzzy plate match carries its edit distance and its confidence for exactly that reason."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 80,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "PTS \u2192 alert latency",
      "description": "The deck's end-to-end figure. On a throttled gateway most of this is the gateway: 92% of the pipeline's wall time was measured blocked upstream, so read it next to the starvation panel on Pipeline Throughput before quoting it as a system latency.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 14,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(saakshi_pts_to_alert_latency_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "live p50",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "format": "time_series",
          "refId": "Z"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(saakshi_pts_to_alert_latency_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "live p95",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "format": "time_series",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "saakshi_alert_pts_latency_seconds",
